WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.802 --> 00:00:07.380
The lights were out for only a few seconds. But that was long enough for

2
00:00:07.381 --> 00:00:15.698
Parker to get hurt. When the lights came on again, Parker was lying onstage, clutching

3
00:00:15.699 --> 00:00:20.284
his knee. A bucket was overturned next to him. Ray was the first one to reach

4
00:00:20.285 --> 00:00:29.277
Parker. "Ow! My knee! I landed on it when I tripped over that bucket!" Parker

5
00:00:29.278 --> 00:00:34.927
moaned with his eyes closed. "You'll be okay," Ray said. "Shake it off and get

6
00:00:34.928 --> 00:00:39.662
back in the game." Parker's eyes flew open. "Get away from me. You—" "I didn't

7
00:00:39.663 --> 00:00:46.096
do anything! I was over there." Ray pointed offstage. "How can you think I'd do

8
00:00:46.097 --> 00:00:52.818
something to hurt you? That's ridiculous! I'd never—" "Everybody out of the way!" Mr. Stein

9
00:00:52.819 --> 00:01:01.238
bounded up the steps to the stage with Ms. Kwan right behind him. "Give him some

10
00:01:01.239 --> 00:01:05.568
room to breathe. Are you all right, Parker?" Parker moaned again. "I can't believe you

11
00:01:05.569 --> 00:01:14.901
did that!" Kyla said to Ray as all the kids stepped back. "I didn't do

12
00:01:14.902 --> 00:01:19.139
anything! I was backstage with you!" "You admitted you told Parker to add some lines!

13
00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:26.633
What were you doing? Trying to steal his part?" "No! Of course not!" But Kyla

14
00:01:26.634 --> 00:01:28.879
wasn't through with him. "You're a real schemer, Ray! You're worse than Rooster! And we

15
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:33.475
all know where he goes in the end. Jail!" Kyla paused for breath. "Lakshmi isn't trying

16
00:01:33.476 --> 00:01:39.713
to hurt Mariah so she can be Annie! You're the worst person in the world,

17
00:01:39.714 --> 00:01:45.778
Ray Aguilera!" "Parker tripped over a bucket," Ray said evenly. "An orphan's bucket. I don't

18
00:01:45.779 --> 00:01:49.544
even have a bucket!" Ray looked at the orphans now surrounding him and Kyla. "One

19
00:01:49.545 --> 00:01:57.359
of you must have left it out there." "Not me!" they all said as one.

20
00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:04.279
"Well . . . well . . . well . . ." Kyla stalled, trying to

21
00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.451
think of what to say. "Then what about the lights?" "The lights? I couldn't turn

22
00:02:07.452 --> 00:02:15.690
off the lights. I was standing right in front of you. I wasn't even near

23
00:02:15.691 --> 00:02:21.847
any lights! The power must have gone off for a minute." Some kids nearby were

24
00:02:21.848 --> 00:02:27.591
muttering, and Ray could tell they were taking Kyla's side. At least the teachers hadn't

25
00:02:27.592 --> 00:02:36.250
heard Kyla. "Why couldn't she stay out of my activities?" he thought. "Why did she

26
00:02:36.251 --> 00:02:43.171
have to try out for this play?" "Lakshmi! Ben!" Ms. Kwan called. "I need you to

27
00:02:43.172 --> 00:02:50.401
get a bag of ice from the cafeteria." "Lakshmi!" Ray pleaded. "You believe me, don't

28
00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:55.899
you?" But she just turned and walked away with Ben. Everyone else abandoned Ray too.

29
00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:04.393
He stood by himself, watching Mr. Stein talk to Parker. Ray knew he'd been wrong

30
00:03:04.394 --> 00:03:09.072
to give Parker bad advice—even as a joke. "But I'd never hurt him!" he said

31
00:03:09.073 --> 00:03:18.645
to himself. By the time Lakshmi and Ben returned with some ice, Parker was sitting up.

32
00:03:18.646 --> 00:03:23.645
After applying ice for a few minutes, he was able to stand with Mr. Stein's

33
00:03:23.646 --> 00:03:34.448
help. Everyone in the auditorium applauded. "Way to go, Parker!" Ray slapped him on the

34
00:03:34.449 --> 00:03:41.792
back as he limped past. "Leave me alone!" Parker snapped. Ray stayed silent, watching as

35
00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:52.620
his friend exited stage left. *** Parker took a few days off from rehearsing to

36
00:03:52.621 --> 00:03:56.696
rest his knee. He still came to rehearsals, but he sat in the auditorium while

37
00:03:56.697 --> 00:04:02.771
Ray played Warbucks. Whenever Ray tried to talk to him, Parker started talking to someone else.

38
00:04:02.772 --> 00:04:08.183
One day Ray looked out from the stage and saw Parker surrounded by girls. They

39
00:04:08.184 --> 00:04:13.839
included Lakshmi, Kyla, and all of Kyla's friends. Ray came offstage in time to hear

40
00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:19.169
Parker explaining that he had to pay attention. "Just in case Ms. Kwan changes one

41
00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:31.330
of the plays onstage." "This isn't soccer," Ray muttered as he passed. "It's called blocking

42
00:04:31.331 --> 00:04:41.569
. That's the right word for how actors move around the stage." "Did he just

43
00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:45.823
call you a blockhead?" Kyla asked. "Who knows?" Parker smiled and shrugged. "Now, who brought me

44
00:04:45.824 --> 00:04:52.054
some cookies today? Those chocolate ones from yesterday were delicious!" Ray rolled his eyes. While

45
00:04:52.055 --> 00:04:55.891
he had lost most of his friends, Parker was making new ones by the minute.

46
00:04:55.892 --> 00:05:04.139
After the break Ray had to rehearse a scene as Officer Ward. He stood in

47
00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:11.384
the wings, waiting for his cue. He watched as Annie sang "Tomorrow" with Sandy. He

48
00:05:11.385 --> 00:05:22.037
wished he could talk to Lakshmi. But what would he say? That his "jokes" had gone

49
00:05:22.038 --> 00:05:27.934
too far? That maybe, if he really thought about it, he had been trying to

50
00:05:27.935 --> 00:05:33.702
steal Parker's role? But he would never do anything to hurt Parker? Yes, that was

51
00:05:33.703 --> 00:05:40.924
perfect. When the orphan and dog stopped singing, Officer Ward entered and confronted them. "Stop

52
00:05:40.925 --> 00:05:47.851
right there!" Ms. Kwan frowned at Ray. "Why are you smiling, Officer Ward? This dog

53
00:05:47.852 --> 00:05:54.351
doesn't have a leash or a license. You're trying to enforce the law here." "Sorry.

54
00:05:54.352 --> 00:06:00.015
I was thinking of something else." "Make your entrance again." Ray went back offstage. This time

55
00:06:00.016 --> 00:06:13.164
he entered as a stern policeman. He looked mean as he threatened to send Sandy

56
00:06:13.165 --> 00:06:23.666
to the dog pound. "Much better, Ray," Ms. Kwan said when they finished the scene.

57
00:06:23.667 --> 00:06:29.895
"That's it for today, everybody." She went over to talk to Parker. Ray waited while

58
00:06:29.896 --> 00:06:36.975
Mr. Stein gave Annie and Sandy a few suggestions to improve their duet. Then, as

59
00:06:36.976 --> 00:06:41.727
Lakshmi left the stage, Ray approached her. "Hey, Lakshmi! Can I talk to you for a

60
00:06:41.728 --> 00:06:47.638
second?" "Grr!" Ray laughed. "Rehearsal is over. You can stop being Sandy now." "Grr!" She

61
00:06:47.639 --> 00:06:53.541
growled at him again and walked away. "But, Lakshmi—" "Attention, everyone!" Ms. Kwan clapped her

62
00:06:53.542 --> 00:07:00.380
hands. "Before you leave, I have some good news. Parker will be back with us

63
00:07:00.381 --> 00:07:09.368
onstage tomorrow. Isn't that right, Parker?" The kids yelled and applauded for Parker. He stood

64
00:07:09.369 --> 00:07:21.936
up and bowed. "I'd also like to thank Ray for taking Parker's place these past

65
00:07:21.937 --> 00:07:32.003
few days." This time not a single cast member clapped. Ms. Kwan looked puzzled. "I know

66
00:07:32.004 --> 00:07:38.253
it's late and you're all tired, but—" "Come on, everybody," said Mr. Stein. "A round

67
00:07:38.254 --> 00:07:50.252
of applause for Ray." There was some weak applause. Mr. Stein looked at Ms. Kwan

68
00:07:50.253 --> 00:07:55.828
and shrugged. By now Ray was rushing toward the exit. "How's Parker doing?" Mrs. Aguilera

69
00:07:55.829 --> 00:08:00.729
asked as Ray and Kyla got into their car. "Everybody's happy that he's coming back

70
00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:04.632
tomorrow," Kyla said. "So, Ray, did you have a good time filling in for Parker?"

71
00:08:04.633 --> 00:08:10.647
"Nope," Ray muttered. "Everybody hates him," Kyla said. Ray shot her a look. Why couldn't she

72
00:08:10.648 --> 00:08:22.459
keep quiet? "What? Explain, please." Mrs. Aguilera turned toward Ray in the backseat. "It's horrible

73
00:08:22.460 --> 00:08:31.343
being the villain in real life," Ray said. "I don't want to talk about it."

